.TH LPM 1 "2026" "lpm v0.9.3" "Ludis Prefix Manager"
.SH NAME
lpm \- prefix manager for Wine/Proton runners and a Lutris game library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lpm
.RI [ command ] " [options] [arguments...]"
.br
.B lpm\-gui
[\fIfile.zgp\fR | \fIfile.zgr\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlpm\fR packages, installs, uninstalls and isolates Windows games running under Wine in Lutris, and manages Wine/Proton runners. Games and runners are exchanged as \fI.zgp\fR (game) and \fI.zgr\fR (runner) archives, produced and consumed locally.
.PP
\fBlpm\fR is a terminal command that can be used in scripts: it never opens a window. Launched with no argument, it shows the help. The graphical interface is started with \fBlpm\-gui\fR (also from the applications menu, or by double-clicking a \fI.zgp\fR or \fI.zgr\fR file).
.PP
This page is a summary. The complete documentation of every command (arguments, options, behavior, exit status, scripting notes, examples) is in the \fIdocs/commands/\fR folder of the project repository.
.SH COMMANDS \(em GAMES
.TP
.B install [\-y] [\-\-allow\-scripts] [\-\-ignore\-hash] <files.zgp...>
Installs games from .zgp archives.
.TP
.B uninstall [\-y] <slugs...>
Uninstalls games.
.TP
.B pack [\-LEVEL] [\-\-hash] <slugs...|\-\-all>
Packages games as .zgp archives.
.TP
.B isolate [\-y] <store|slug>
Splits a shared store prefix (Epic, EA, Ubisoft, Battle.net) into one prefix per game (beta).
.TP
.B list, list\-isolable
Lists installed games / games sharing a store prefix.
.TP
.B info <slug>
Shows the metadata of an installed game.
.TP
.B create\-prefix [\-y] <names...>
Creates empty Wine prefixes registered in Lutris.
.TP
.B exe\-install [\-y] <file>
Creates a prefix and runs a Windows installer in it.
.TP
.B shortcut <slugs...|\-\-all>
(Re)creates menu/desktop shortcuts.
.TP
.B icon, splash, logo <slugs...|\-\-all>
Fetches images from SteamGridDB (personal API key required).
.TP
.B sync\-media <slugs...|\-\-all>
Downloads Lutris's own media for games that lack them.
.TP
.B tools <slug> <tool> [args]
Runs a Wine tool on a game (winetricks, regedit, winecfg, console, exe, folder, favorite, env, runner, mangohud, gamepad).
.TP
.B vsync status | <slug> [status|on|off] [setting...]
Forces VSync off for a game with environment variables (d3d9, d3d11, d3d12, gl\-nvidia, gl\-mesa; none given = all).
.TP
.B lsfg <slugs...> on|off, lsfg status
Enables/disables lsfg-vk frame generation.
.TP
.B launcher <slugs...> on|off
Enables/disables the LPM Launcher (loading screen and executable picker).
.TP
.B launcher\-entries <slug> get|set
Reads/replaces the launcher's picker entries (JSON).
.TP
.B killwine [\-y]
Kills every running Wine/Proton process.
.SH COMMANDS \(em RUNNERS
.TP
.B install\-runner [\-y] <files.zgr|names...>
Installs runners from local archives or the GitHub release.
.TP
.B uninstall\-runner [\-y] <names...>
Uninstalls runners.
.TP
.B pack\-runner [\-LEVEL] [\-\-hash] <names...|\-\-all>
Packages runners as .zgr archives.
.TP
.B list\-runner, list\-remote\-runners
Lists installed / remotely available runners.
.SH COMMANDS \(em SYSTEM
.TP
.B check
Checks that the runners needed by installed games are present and fetches missing ones.
.TP
.B lutris\-version [flatpak|native|reset]
Shows/forces the Lutris installation used when both exist.
.TP
.B self\-update [check|install]
Checks for a newer lpm release and installs it (package installs only).
.TP
.B log [\-n N|\-\-all|\-\-grep PATTERN|\-\-clear]
Shows, filters or clears the action log.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-y
Automatically answers yes to the command's general confirmation question (it does not skip the hash and embedded-script questions).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-scripts
install: accepts embedded launch/close scripts of a .zgp without asking (only for packages you trust).
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-hash
install, install\-runner: skips the sha256 sidecar check.
.TP
.B \-\-hash
pack, pack\-runner: writes a sha256 sidecar file next to each archive.
.TP
.B \-0 \&... \-22
pack, pack\-runner: zstd compression level.
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-v
Shows the lpm version.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Shows this page (or a built-in summary if it is not installed).
.PP
Global options must be placed right after the command name, before its other arguments (for example \fBlpm install \-y game.zgp\fR).
.SH LOG
Errors printed by commands, and some successes, are recorded in \fI~/.local/share/lpm/lpm.log\fR (always under the home directory), one line per event with four tab-separated columns: timestamp, origin, status (OK, ERROR, WARN or INFO), detail. Past 10000 lines the file is renamed \fIlpm.log.1\fR and a fresh log is started. See \fBlog\fR above.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/lpm/lpm.log
Action log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/lpm/
lpm configuration (SteamGridDB key, Lutris version choice, lsfg\-vk).
.TP
.I <game_dir>/lpm\-launcher.yml
Launcher picker entries.
.TP
.I ~/.config/lutris/ (native package) / ~/.var/app/net.lutris.Lutris/ (Flatpak)
Lutris configuration and database, read and modified by lpm.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project repository (https://github.com/RogerBytes/lpm), folder \fIdocs/commands/\fR: one page per command, the global options (\fIoptions.md\fR) and the archive formats (\fIarchives.md\fR).
.SH AUTHOR
Ludis Prefix Manager (lpm) is a personal project.
